## Best Practices

- **Containers**: All services run in Docker. Main stack: `docker/docker-compose.yml`. ERPNext: `erpnext/frappe_docker/`. Mailcow: `mailcow/`. Tactical RMM: `tactical/`. Run `startup-all.bat` from Dashboard root.
- **Domain**: Stack runs on `kecktech.net` throughout all configs. Do NOT migrate to `kecktech.io` without explicit confirmation — every service config would need updating.
- **Test environment**: Traefik with same hostnames as production. Add `127.0.0.1` entries in `hosts` for all `*.kecktech.net` names. Do not configure Cloudflare until Phase 8.
- **Production (when ready)**: Cloudflare Tunnel for **public-facing apps only** (`kecktech.net`, `help.kecktech.net`, `tickets.kecktech.net`). All internal/staff apps remain Tailscale-only. Zero open inbound ports.
- **App-to-app communication**: Prefer webhooks and REST APIs. Document every integration in INTEGRATIONS.md.
- **Secrets**: Store in `docker/.env` (gitignored). Reference in compose as env vars.
- **SSO exception**: LLDAP 0.6.x OPAQUE bug — `!` in passwords fails LDAP bind. SSO credential is `keckadmin` / `Kecktech2026` (no `!`). All other app logins use `Kecktech2026!`. Do not change until upstream fixes the bug.
- **Accessibility**: WikiJS and WordPress public pages must support high-contrast (WCAG AAA) and 18px+ font for senior visitors. Internal operator tools are exempt.

## Integration Points

1. **Lead → Ticket**: WordPress contact form → Zammad ticket (email to tickets@kecktech.net)
2. **Ticket → Dispatch**: High-priority Zammad ticket → n8n → Twilio SMS to on-call tech
3. **RMM → Ticket**: Tactical RMM critical alert → n8n → Zammad API `POST /api/v1/tickets`
4. **Billing**: All invoicing in ERPNext; Stripe for collection (ACH/CC)
5. **Analytics**: Umami tracking on WordPress + WikiJS
6. **Single dashboard**: Next.js at dashboard.kecktech.net — health tiles for all 12 services

## Conventions

- **Config as code**: Compose files and app configs live in version control.
- **Document in PROJECT_PLAN.md + REMAINING-TASKS.md**: Any new phase or step gets a clear entry.
- **No mock data** in production paths unless explicitly requested.
- **Windows dev**: Development on Windows 11; target production is Linux VM. Use cross-platform commands or document OS-specific steps.

# Kecktech Development Rules

You are assisting Jon (GitHub: Bizzo1975) with Kecktech platform services and custom application development. All work follows the Bizzo Development Workflow Framework (10-stage lifecycle, 5-project max).

## Tech Stack (Non-Negotiable)
- TypeScript strict mode — no `any` without explicit justification
- Next.js 14+ with App Router
- PostgreSQL + Prisma ORM (no raw SQL except migrations)
- NextAuth.js for auth (OAuth, credentials, SSO-ready)
- Tailwind CSS (client-themeable via CSS variables)
- Docker Compose for deployment
- Self-hosted on Proxmox — never default to cloud SaaS

## Code Standards
- UUIDs for primary keys
- `createdAt`/`updatedAt` on all tables
- Soft deletes (`deletedAt`) for user-facing data
- Error boundaries and graceful error handling
- Loading states for all async operations
- Mobile-first responsive design (320px-1920px)
- API-first: all business logic via typed API routes
- No hardcoded credentials — environment variables only

## File Conventions
- Components: PascalCase (`ContactCard.tsx`)
- Utilities: camelCase (`formatCurrency.ts`)
- API routes: kebab-case directories (`/api/purchase-orders/`)
- Prisma models: PascalCase singular (`model Invoice {}`)

## When Writing Code
1. Start with the Prisma schema if touching data models
2. Build API routes with input validation (zod preferred)
3. Create reusable components — check if similar exists first
4. Include proper TypeScript types for all props and returns
5. Add JSDoc comments on exported functions
6. Handle loading, error, and empty states in all UI

## Project Context Files
- `prompts/PROJECT-CONTEXT.md` — Master context (read first)
- `prompts/platform-services/` — BookStack, PeerTube, Rocket.Chat prompts
- `prompts/custom-apps/01-10` — Individual app specifications with data models

## Security Checklist (Every Feature)
- [ ] Input validation on all user inputs
- [ ] RBAC check on protected routes
- [ ] CSRF protection on mutations
- [ ] Rate limiting on public endpoints
- [ ] No secrets in code or logs
- [ ] SQL injection prevention (Prisma handles this)
- [ ] XSS prevention (React handles most, sanitize rich text)

